{"id":"QAAMUUS-DET-001","source":"Qaamuuska Af-Soomaaliga (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","section":"Naxwaha af-soomaaliga oo kooban — Cayimayaasha","topic":"determiner_classes","rule":"The grammar groups determiners (cayimayaal) into four semantic-functional classes: articles (qodobo), demonstratives (tilmaameyaal), interrogative determiners (weyddiimo), and possessives (lahaansho).","status":"source_backed","executable":false}
{"id":"QAAMUUS-DET-002","source":"Qaamuuska Af-Soomaaliga (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","section":"Naxwaha af-soomaaliga oo kooban — Cayimayaasha","topic":"gender_agreement","rule":"Determiner suffixes distinguish masculine and feminine forms: masculine forms begin with -k and feminine forms with -t, agreeing with the grammatical gender of the noun they attach to.","status":"source_backed","executable":false}
{"id":"QAAMUUS-DET-003","source":"Qaamuuska Af-Soomaaliga (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","section":"Qodobbada","topic":"masculine_definite_article","rule":"The masculine definite article is represented by -ka, with phonologically conditioned surface variants including -ga, -ha, and -a.","examples":[{"analysis":"nin + ka","surface":"ninka"},{"analysis":"buug + ka","surface":"buugga"}],"status":"source_backed","executable":false}
{"id":"QAAMUUS-DET-004","source":"Qaamuuska Af-Soomaaliga (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","section":"Qodobbada","topic":"feminine_definite_article_allomorphy","rule":"The feminine article begins from -ta and undergoes phonological changes after some noun-final sounds.","examples":[{"analysis":"maro + ta","surface":"marada","change":"t_to_d"},{"analysis":"bad + ta","surface":"badda","change":"t_to_d"},{"analysis":"qodax + ta","surface":"qodaxda","change":"t_to_d"},{"analysis":"bac + ta","surface":"bacda","change":"t_to_d"},{"analysis":"gallay + ta","surface":"gallayda","change":"t_to_d"},{"analysis":"bu' + ta","surface":"bu'da","change":"t_to_d"},{"analysis":"ul + ta","surface":"usha","change":"t_to_sh_after_l"},{"analysis":"il + ta","surface":"isha","change":"t_to_sh_after_l"},{"analysis":"bil + ta","surface":"bisha","change":"t_to_sh_after_l"},{"analysis":"dhal + ta","surface":"dhasha","change":"t_to_sh_after_l"}],"status":"source_backed","executable":false}
{"id":"QAAMUUS-DET-005","source":"Qaamuuska Af-Soomaaliga (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","section":"Dibkabayaasha tilmaamayaasha","topic":"demonstratives","rule":"Demonstrative suffixes encode three distance/orientation distinctions and distinguish masculine from feminine.","forms":{"near":{"masculine":"-kan","feminine":"-tan"},"far":{"masculine":"-kas","feminine":"-tas"},"lateral_or_more_remote":{"masculine":"-keer","feminine":"-teer"}},"examples":["Ninkan ayaa iska leh baabuurka","Gabdhahaas ayaa u socda dugsiga","Wiilkeer baa arday ah"],"status":"source_backed","executable":false}
{"id":"QAAMUUS-DET-006","source":"Qaamuuska Af-Soomaaliga (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","section":"Dibkabayaasha lahaanshaha","topic":"possessive_suffixes","rule":"Possessive suffixes distinguish possessor person/number and noun gender.","forms":{"1sg":{"masculine":"-kayga","feminine":"-tayda"},"2sg":{"masculine":"-kaada","feminine":"-taada"},"3sg_masc_possessor":{"masculine":"-kiisa","feminine":"-tiisa"},"3sg_fem_possessor":{"masculine":"-keeda","feminine":"-teeda"},"1pl_exclusive":{"masculine":"-kaayaga","feminine":"-taayada"},"1pl_inclusive":{"masculine":"-keenna","feminine":"-teenna"},"2pl":{"masculine":"-kiinna","feminine":"-tiinna"},"3pl":{"masculine":"-kooda","feminine":"-tooda"}},"examples":[{"analysis":"buug + kayga","surface":"buuggayga"},{"analysis":"arday + tiisa","surface":"ardaydiisa"},{"analysis":"dal + keenna","surface":"dalkeenna"},{"analysis":"ul + tiinna","surface":"ushiinna"}],"status":"source_backed","executable":false}
{"id":"QAAMUUS-DET-007","source":"Qaamuuska Af-Soomaaliga (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","topic":"word_analyzer_implication","rule":"A future analyzer should segment attached determiner morphology and return both the base noun and the attached article/demonstrative/possessive information rather than treating the full surface form as an unrelated lemma.","examples":[{"surface":"buugga","target_analysis":"buug + masculine definite article"},{"surface":"marada","target_analysis":"maro + feminine definite article"},{"surface":"buuggayga","target_analysis":"buug + 1sg possessive + article structure"}],"status":"project_schema_implication","executable":false}
